Title: The Cellar Door
Credit: Written by
Author: Previz Stage
Draft date: 2026-10-24

INT. FARMHOUSE CELLAR - NIGHT

A low stone cellar. Rotting shelves of preserve jars, a dirt floor, one bare bulb swinging on its cord. Water drips somewhere in the dark. The far wall has a door that is far too new for the house.

JUNE (30s, pale, dark hair scraped back, a grey rain jacket zipped to the chin, muddy boots) stands at the bottom of the stairs with a flashlight.

CAL (30s, heavy-set, ginger beard, flannel shirt, a tyre iron in one hand) comes down behind her, slowly.

CAL
Nobody built that. It wasn't there Tuesday.

JUNE
(whispering)
It's warm. The handle's warm.

CAL
June. Don't.

JUNE
Something on the other side is breathing.

EXT. CORNFIELD - NIGHT

Dead corn under a sickle moon. A rusted scarecrow on a cross. Fog pours in low from the tree line. A black dog trots along the edge of the field and stops to stare.

June runs out of the rows, flashlight dying. Cal stumbles after her.

CAL
Keep going, the truck's past the fence!

JUNE
(stopping dead)
Cal. The truck is gone.

CAL
That's not possible.

JUNE
Neither was the door.
